# Dongle names
␀␀␀␀# Dongle names␀␀.LOCK␀␀␀ / ␀/ADF/SAMPLE␀/ADF/SAMPLE/Sample.adf␀␀/ADF/SAMPLE/Sample.nfo␀␀This placeholder shows WHERE your disk image goes.
A real game is an .adf disk image (usually 880KB for Amiga).
The browser ignores any folder named SAMPLE - copy the layout,
don't play in here.
␀/ADF/SAMPLE/Sample.jpg␀␀Title: Sample Game Name
Blurb: 1991 - Publisher Name - one line about the game

This folder is an EXAMPLE ONLY - the browser ignores any folder
named SAMPLE. Copy this layout for real games:

  /ADF/YourGame/YourGame.adf   the disk image
  /ADF/YourGame/YourGame.jpg   cover art (JPEG or PNG, any size)
  /ADF/YourGame/YourGame.nfo   this info file (plain text)
  /ADF/YourGame/YourGame.rtfm  how-to-play manual (plain text, optional)

NFO rules:
  'Title:' overrides the display name (any case: TITLE:/title:).
  'Blurb:' or 'Description:' = info text shown on the cover panel.
  Or skip the labels: first line = title, following lines = blurb.

Multi-disk games: YourGame-1.adf, YourGame-2.adf, ...
Same pattern applies in /DSK for .dsk images.
␀␀␀/ADF/SAMPLE/Sample.rtfm␀HOW TO PLAY - and how this MANUAL works
=======================================

You are reading the GTi manual viewer. This text came
from a plain-text file sitting next to the game:

  /ADF/SAMPLE/Sample.rtfm

Any game can have one. Drop a file named the same as
the disk, ending in .rtfm, beside it:

  /ADF/YourGame/YourGame.rtfm

...and a little book button appears on the cover art.
Tap it to read the game's instructions - controls,
cheats, copy-protection answers, whatever you like.

USING THE READER
  - Drag up or down to scroll; flick for a fast spin.
  - SIZE cycles SMALL / NORMAL / LARGE text, following
    your menu font setting.
  - CLOSE (or tap the page) returns to the library.

TIPS
  - Keep it plain ASCII text. Accents and smart quotes
    are cleaned up for you, but plain is safest.
  - Blank lines make paragraphs. Short lines read best.
  - Manuals are meant to be short and handy - a page or
    two of how-to-play basics.

Read the fine manual. :)

- OMEGAWARE
